From 68280c2e2d874a0085feb83797cda54acbea6aef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forest <forest@localhost>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 17:44:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] pds: device-signed two-phase write, and folders made from
 a device-made DID

Two procedures under foundation.forest.host, both authenticated by a
service token the device signs with the folder's own key:

prepareCommit applies the writes to the folder's tree without storing
anything and returns the unsigned commit bytes, the rev, the head it
builds on, and the writes with record keys filled in.

submitCommit rebuilds the same commit from the same writes and rev,
checks the signature against the DID document's signing key, checks it
builds on the current head (swapCommit as in applyWrites; the rev must
be newer than the head's, which is what refuses a replay), and stores
it. Nothing is kept between the two phases.

When the DID has no folder on this host, the commit is the genesis and
submitting it creates the folder: the DID document must point at this
host and name a handle; no email, password, session, or key file.

The transactor's pre-commit checks are shared between the server-signed
path (unchanged in behaviour) and the device-signed one.
